{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "avg-03-weighted-and-frequency-averages",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Weighted and Frequency Averages",
    "description": "Average values that occur different numbers of times or carry different importance by turning each value into its total contribution.",
    "teachingApproach": "Begin with repeated values so weighting feels like counting copies, then move to unequal group sizes, grouped-frequency midpoints, exam and subject weights, quantity-weighted prices and an unknown weighted component. Repeatedly show value × weight before division so learners see why a simple mean of displayed subgroup means can fail.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "Teach weighted average as total contribution divided by total weight. Build from repeated values to unequal group sizes, frequency tables using class midpoints, examination weights, subject weights and quantities bought at different unit prices. Show why simply averaging subgroup means works only when their weights are equal. Include an unknown weighted component where the overall mean is known. The learner should repeatedly use value × weight, add the contributions, add the weights, then divide once."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn what an average does when some values count more than others.\n\nThe rule is simple: a value that appears five times must contribute five times as much to the total as a value that appears once.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose three tests scored 70 and two tests scored 80. The value 70 appears three times; 80 appears twice.\n\nSo the total contribution is:\n3 × 70 + 2 × 80 = 370",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "There are 5 tests, so the weighted average is:\n\n370 ÷ 5 = 74\n\nThink 'value × how many times it counts' before dividing.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
