    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Why is the simple average of subgroup means dangerous?\n\nTwo people average 40 and eight people average 70. The two displayed means are 40 and 70, but they do not have equal weight.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Combined mean = (2×40 + 8×70) ÷ 10\n= 640 ÷ 10\n= 64\n\nThe simple mean 55 would be correct only if both groups had the same number of people.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
